## Circuit geometry

The circuit centrelines traced from OpenStreetMap are **ODbL 1.0**, which is
share-alike and carries a database right reaching the whole database its data
lands in. They are therefore **not in `f1.db`** and not covered by this
licence: they are published as `f1-geometry.db` alongside it, under ODbL, (c)
OpenStreetMap contributors. Two databases distributed side by side are a
Collective Database, which ODbL does not treat as derivative. See
ATTRIBUTION.md and tools/geometry_overlay.py.

Part of the history predates that split. **Every commit whose `f1.db` has rows
in `circuit_geometry`** — thirty-five of them, in ten distinct versions of the
file, dated 2026-09-05 to 2026-09-09 and all ancestors of `6610b6da` ("Merge
the licence enforcement and the ODbL split") — carries the twenty-five
centrelines inside `f1.db` itself, which makes each of those files a
Derivative Database.

They are offered as such: **ODbL 1.0, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors**, **in
addition to** the terms above rather than in place of them. Share-alike runs
with the Wikipedia-derived rows and this project's own prose in the same file
whatever else that file acquires, so both obligations apply together and
neither displaces the other.

The boundary is that merge and not the split commit `5a70558`, which was
parallel work: eight of the thirty-five are later than it by the clock and
reached the trunk only when it was merged. No commit from `6610b6da` onward
has a row in `circuit_geometry` in `f1.db`. The historical files are kept
rather than rewritten out, because the history of a licence decision is part
of the record.

Three files in the repository's harvest/ hold OpenStreetMap data. They are
**ODbL 1.0, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors**, and are not covered by this
licence, which covers the rest of harvest/:

  - `harvest/circuit_geometry.txt` — the centrelines themselves, which
    f1-geometry.db is built from.
  - `harvest/circuit_geometry.log` — the OpenStreetMap relation each circuit
    was admitted on, and the length measured from its geometry.
  - `harvest/circuit_wikidata.txt` — the candidate relations for each
    circuit, and the length measured from each one's geometry.

The Wikidata item ids in circuit_wikidata.txt's wikidata_id column stay
CC0, as its header says.

## Live timing data

tools/fastf1_load.py optionally loads per-lap timing, stints, pit stops, race
control messages and team radio from the Formula 1 live timing API via
FastF1. That data belongs to Formula One Management and is not covered by
this licence, is not redistributed, and is not committed to this repository
— the relevant tables are empty in the committed database and are filled
only locally when you run the loader yourself. `verify.py` enforces this
rather than trusting it; see ATTRIBUTION.md for what is checked and for the
two tables where the rule is by source rather than by emptiness.
